n weight.  A function with weight at most 5 cannot dominate $P_8$ due to the limited number of vertices each label-2 or label-1 vertex can cover.  Each vertex labeled 2 can dominate at most its degree plus 1.\n\n**Extending radius to weight constraint**\n\nConsidering graphs with a given radius $R$, exploring if a weight bound of $W \\le R$ is possible. Observed that a graph with radius $R$ always contains a path of at least length $R$.  For a shortest path of length $2R$, two vertices at a distance of 3 or more cannot be dominated by the same label 2 vertex.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"manage_subagents","args":{"Action":"list","toolAction":"Listing subagents","toolSummary":"Check subagent status"}}]}
