nd leading space.\\n1: #!/bin/bash\\n2: # check.sh — the ONLY command an agent may run.\\n3: #\\n4: #   /abs/path/tools/antigravity/check.sh FILE.lean\\n5: #\\n6: # Lives outside every agent workspace and is hashed by guard.sh: agents can\\n7: # write inside their workspace, so a checker kept there could be rewritten into\\n8: # anything. It screens the file first (tools/antigravity_handoff.py lint), because\\n9: # Lean elaboration can itself run shell commands; then elaborates it with bare\\n10: # `lean` and an explicit LEAN_PATH, and prints every theorem's axioms. Nothing\\n11: # here depends on $HOME — agents run under a private one — and `lake` is never\\n12: # involved (in this project lake deletes Mathlib when it cannot re-clone).\\n13: set -uo pipefail\\n14: f=\\\"${1:?usage: check.sh FILE.lean}\\\"\\n15: [ -f \\\"$f\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: no such file: $f\\\"; exit 2; }\\n16: \\n17: ROOT=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"$(readlink -f \\\"$0\\\")\\\")/../..\\\" && pwd)\\\"\\n18: # Tool paths come from a protected file, not from the home directory: agents run\\n19: # under a private HOME, and on compute nodes `getent passwd` reports a different\\n20: # home (/home/<user>@ad…) than the one the tools live in.\\n21: ENVF=\\\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_env\\\"\\n22: export ELAN_HOME=\\\"$(grep -m1 '^AGF_ELAN_HOME=' \\\"$ENVF\\\" 2>/dev/null | cut -d= -f2-)\\\"\\n23: LEAN=\\\"$ELAN_HOME/bin/lean\\\"\\n24: [ -x \\\"$LEAN\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: lean not found (ELAN_HOME='$ELAN_HOME' from $ENVF)\\\"; exit 2; }\\n25: PY=\\\"$ROOT/.venv/bin/python\\\"\\n26: LP_FILE=\\\"$ROOT/handoff/.agf_lean_path\\\"\\n27: [ -s \\\"$LP_FILE\\\" ] || { echo \\\"CHECK: missing $LP_FILE\\\"; exit 2; }\\n28: export LEAN_PATH=\\\"$(cat \\\"$LP_FILE\\\")\\\"\\n29: \\n30: orig=\\\"$(ls \\\"$ROOT\\\"/benchmark/challenges_*/\\\"$(basename \\\"$f\\\")\\\" 2>/dev/null | head -1)\\\"\\n31: if ! \\\"$PY\\\" \\\"$ROOT/tools/antigravity_handoff.py\\\" lint ${orig:+--original \\\"$orig\\\"} \\\"$f\\\"; then\\n32:   echo \\\"CHECK: refused to elaborate — remove the construct named above.\\\"\\n33:   exit 3\\n34: fi\\n35: \\n36: tmp=\\\"$(mktemp --suffix=.lean)\\\"\\n37: cp \\\"$f\\\" \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n38: for t in $(grep -oE '^theorem +[A-Za-z0-9_]+' \\\"$f\\\" | awk '{print $2}'); do\\n39:   echo \\\"#print axioms $t\\\" >> \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n40: done\\n41: timeout 1800 \\\"$LEAN\\\" \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n42: rc=$?\\n43: rm -f \\\"$tmp\\\"\\n44: if [ $rc -eq 0 ]; then\\n45:   echo \\\"CHECK: elaborated. Allowed axioms: propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound.\\\"\\n46:   echo \\\"       'sorryAx' in a list above means that theorem is unfinished.\\\"\\n47: else\\n48:   echo \\\"CHECK: FAILED (exit $rc)\\\"\\n49: fi\\n50: exit $rc\\n51: \\nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\\n\"}\n39: {\"step_index\":38,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-09-11T14:50:08Z\",\"thinking\":\"**Assessing command execution capabilities**\\n\\nThe provided script likely relies on shell commands. The immediate need is confirming if a command execution tool is available. The tool declarations are being reviewed to determine if a bash-like environment is accessible.\\n\\n\\n**Evaluating subagent capabilities**\\n\\nDirect shell command execution isn't available at the top level; thus, need to assess subagent functionalities. The subagent descriptions are being reviewed to determine if any possess command execution abilities, particularly focusing on the `teamwork_preview_follower`. The user request's target file and checker script are also reviewed for context.\\n\\n\\n\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"list_dir\",\"args\":{\"DirectoryPath\":\"\\\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing\\\"\",\"toolAction\":\"\\\"Listing GraphConjecturing root\\\"\",\"toolSummary\":\"\\\"List GraphConjecturing directory\\\"\"}}]}\n40: {\"step_index\":39,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"GENERIC\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_